{"id":"route53","corpus":"aws","title":"Amazon Route 53","sourceUrl":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/Welcome.html","license":"AWS Documentation © Amazon Web Services, Inc.","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"Amazon Route 53"},{"kind":"p","text":"Amazon Route 53 is a highly available and scalable Domain Name System (DNS) web service. You can use Route 53 to perform three main functions in any combination: domain registration, DNS routing, and health checking."},{"kind":"p","text":"If you choose to use Route 53 for all three functions, follow the order below:"},{"kind":"p","text":"1. Register domain names"},{"kind":"p","text":"Your website needs a name, such as example.com. With Route 53, you can register a name for your website or web application, known as a domain name."},{"kind":"li","text":"For an overview, see How domain registration works."},{"kind":"li","text":"For a procedure, see Registering a new domain."},{"kind":"li","text":"For a tutorial that takes you through registering a domain and creating a simple website in an Amazon S3 bucket, see Getting started with Amazon Route 53."},{"kind":"p","text":"2. Route internet traffic to the resources for your domain"},{"kind":"p","text":"When a user opens a web browser and enters your domain name (example.com) or subdomain name (acme.example.com), Route 53 connects the browser with your website or web application."},{"kind":"li","text":"For an overview, see How internet traffic is routed to your website or web application."},{"kind":"li","text":"For procedures, see Configuring Amazon Route 53 as your DNS service."},{"kind":"li","text":"For a procedure on how to route email to Amazon WorkMail, see Routing traffic to Amazon WorkMail."},{"kind":"p","text":"3. Check the health of your resources"},{"kind":"p","text":"Route 53 sends automated requests over the internet to a resource, such as a web server, to verify that it's reachable, available, and functional. You can receive notifications when a resource becomes unavailable. You can also route internet traffic away from unhealthy resources."},{"kind":"li","text":"For an overview, see How Amazon Route 53 checks the health of your resources."},{"kind":"li","text":"For procedures, see Creating Amazon Route 53 health checks."},{"kind":"h3","text":"Other Route 53 features"},{"kind":"p","text":"In addition to being a Domain Name System (DNS) web service, Route 53 offers the following features:"},{"kind":"p","text":"VPC Resolver"},{"kind":"p","text":"Get recursive DNS for your Amazon VPCs in AWS Regions, VPCs in AWS Outposts racks, or any other on-premises networks. Create conditional forwarding rules and Route 53 endpoints to resolve custom names in Route 53 private hosted zones or in your on-premises DNS servers."},{"kind":"p","text":"For more information , see What is Route 53 VPC Resolver?."},{"kind":"p","text":"Amazon Route 53 Resolver on Outposts"},{"kind":"p","text":"Connect VPC Resolver on Outpost racks with DNS servers in your on-premises data centers through Resolver endpoints. This resolves DNS queries between the Outposts racks and your other on-premises resources."},{"kind":"p","text":"For more information , see What is Amazon Route 53 on Outposts?."},{"kind":"p","text":"Resolver DNS Firewall"},{"kind":"p","text":"Protect your recursive DNS queries within the VPC Resolver. Create domain lists and build firewall rules that filter outbound DNS traffic against these rules."},{"kind":"p","text":"For more information , see Using DNS Firewall to filter outbound DNS traffic."},{"kind":"p","text":"Traffic Flow"},{"kind":"p","text":"Easy-to-use and cost-effective global traffic management: route end users to the best endpoint for your application based on geoproximity, latency, health, and other considerations."},{"kind":"p","text":"For more information , see Using Traffic Flow to route DNS traffic."},{"kind":"p","text":"Amazon Route 53 Profiles"},{"kind":"p","text":"With Route 53 Profiles, you can apply and manage DNS-related Route 53 configurations across many VPCs and in different AWS account."},{"kind":"p","text":"For more information , see What are Amazon Route 53 Profiles?."}],"lemmas":{"amazons":["amazon","amazons"],"routes":["route","routes"],"highlies":["highlies","highly"],"availables":["availables","available"],"scalables":["scalables","scalable"],"domains":["domain","domains"],"naming":["naming","name"],"named":["named","name"],"systems":["system","systems"],"webs":["web","webs"],"services":["service","services"],"serviced":["serviced","service"],"servicing":["servicing","service"],"uses":["use","uses"],"used":["used","use"],"performs":["performs","perform"],"performing":["performing","perform"],"performed":["performed","perform"],"threes":["three","threes"],"mains":["main","mains"],"functions":["function","functions"],"functioned":["functioned","function"],"functioning":["functioning","function"],"combinations":["combination","combinations"],"registrations":["registration","registrations"],"routing":["routing","rout"],"routings":["routings","routing"],"routs":["rout","routs"],"checking":["checking","check"],"checkings":["checkings","checking"],"checked":["checked","check"],"chooses":["chooses","choose"],"choosing":["choosing","choose"],"chose":["chose","choose"],"chosen":["chosen","choose"],"follows":["follows","follow"],"followed":["followed","follow"],"orders":["order","orders"],"ordered":["ordered","order"],"ordering":["ordering","order"],"belows":["belows","below"],"registers":["register","registers"],"registered":["registered","register"],"names":["name","names"],"websites":["website","websites"],"needs":["need","needs"],"needed":["needed","need"],"needing":["needing","need"],"examples":["example","examples"],"coms":["coms","com"],"applications":["application","applications"],"known":["known","know"],"knowns":["knowns","known"],"knows":["know","knows"],"knowed":["knowed","know"],"knowing":["knowing","know"],"knew":["knew","know"],"overviews":["overview"